00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:11,960
 Real quick recap before we finish up, whenever you're working with the iterator variable

59
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:15,480
 itself within a for loop, always make a copy.

60
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:17,680
 So in this case, we're making a copy of rooms.

61
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:22,440
 So we're using i here, so we need to make a copy of whatever we're using it with.

62
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:26,320
 And if we don't do that, then you will for sure run into some bugs later.

63
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:30,920
 So always make sure whenever you utilize the iterator variable within a loop, you're making

64
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:32,160
 it in the context of a copy.

65
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,560
 So we're copying room in this case.

66
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:39,080
 And even if you just want the variable by itself without indexing an array, you still want

67
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:40,680
 to make a copy of it.

68
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:45,480
 So for example, you can just do something like this.

